claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:

> This builds the hub that "[PATCH v2] jails/instances/lab-mail: Spec
> the list's mail hub" [1] describes, now on b/dev. It turns the relay
> jail into the list's home: OpenSMTPD takes posts, Dovecot holds and
> serves the list, and mbsync keeps it in sync with Fastmail.
>
> Patch 1 revises the spec on two points that turned up while building
> it. LMTP alone files only into INBOX, so a Sieve script from Pigeonhole
> puts each post into lists. And Dovecot answers OK to a reader's STORE
> and EXPUNGE without changing anything, rather than refusing them, so
> the rights section and acceptance step 7 now say so.
>
> Patch 2 is the implementation.

The Sieve idea is interesting, and I'm not opposed to it... but it's
different from what was originally specced. So it should go in a follow
up commit.

Basically I would like to see the implementation as we discussed, and
then since sieve is a new proposal it can just be a commit on top of
this. That way I can see what the specific difference is.

I'm fine with the basic behavior being to only deliver to inbox. Then I
can see if it's worth adding sieve.

Also the commit messages are wordy, they should probably be more
list-like when there are several changes in there. A commit message
should be mostly "why", but any "what" should probably be bullet points.
